+### 3.2 Section rhythm — the rule the page did not have
+
+Light sections **strictly alternate** between two surfaces, and full-bleed dark
+bands are the chapter breaks between them.
+
+| step | class | surface |
+|---|---|---|
+| base | `.section` | `--bg` |
+| tint | `.section--tint` | `--surface-1` + the paper texture |
+| break | `.photo-bg-section`, `.wood-grain-dark` | full-bleed dark |
+
+Homepage, in order: hero **DARK** → gallery base → services **DARK** → process
+tint → craft base → design tint → reviews base → faq tint → pricing base →
+library tint → quote **DARK** → footer **DARK**.
+
+Before this the order was tint, DARK, base, base, base, tint, base, base, tint,
+DARK — three base sections in a row, with a 0.4% lightness difference doing the
+work of a rhythm. A difference that small either reads as a mistake or is not
+seen at all.
+
+**A new section takes whichever step its neighbour is not.** That is the whole
+rule; if a section cannot say which step it is, it is in the wrong place.
+
